 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The oldest light in the universe is all around you, and two men blamed it on pigeon poop.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 121
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "New Jersey, nineteen sixty-four. Arno Penzias and Robert Wilson had a giant horn antenna.",
   "from": 125,
   "to": 267
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They wanted to hear the Milky Way.",
   "from": 271,
   "to": 308
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But their receiver picked up a faint, steady hiss.",
   "from": 311,
   "to": 389
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Day or night, wherever they aimed, the hiss stayed the same.",
   "from": 392,
   "to": 465
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They aimed it at New York City. Same hiss.",
   "from": 469,
   "to": 539
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then they looked inside the horn. Two pigeons were nesting there.",
   "from": 542,
   "to": 631
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "penzias",
   "text": "And a layer of white dielectric substance!",
   "from": 635,
   "to": 725
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That's science talk for pigeon poop.",
   "from": 728,
   "to": 770
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They scrubbed the horn clean and sent the pigeons away.",
   "from": 774,
   "to": 837
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Two days later, the pigeons were back. Accounts differ on how they left.",
   "from": 840,
   "to": 926
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And the hiss? It never changed at all.",
   "from": 930,
   "to": 987
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So what hisses from every direction at once?",
   "from": 991,
   "to": 1055
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, the universe began hot and bright, in the Big Bang.",
   "from": 1070,
   "to": 1165
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "As space stretched, that glow cooled into faint microwaves, three degrees above absolute zero.",
   "from": 1169,
   "to": 1294
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "It fills the whole sky, so the horn heard it everywhere.",
   "from": 1298,
   "to": 1399
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In Princeton, Robert Dicke's team was about to look for that glow.",
   "from": 1403,
   "to": 1477
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "dicke",
   "text": "We've been scooped.",
   "from": 1481,
   "to": 1511
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In nineteen seventy-eight, Penzias and Wilson won the Nobel Prize in Physics.",
   "from": 1515,
   "to": 1645
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They went looking for pigeon poop, and found the dawn of time.",
   "from": 1648,
   "to": 1729
  }
 ],
